; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
; .npmrc.publish — TEMPLATE, not read by pnpm.
;
; `scripts/release.mjs` renders this into a TRANSIENT workspace-root `.npmrc`
; for the duration of a publish, then restores/removes it. It is a template
; (and there is no committed `.npmrc`) for two reasons:
;
;   1. The auth token must never be committed. It only ever exists in the
;      transient file, at mode 0600, and is removed in a `finally`.
;   2. A committed `.npmrc` carrying `${FAMS_NPM_REGISTRY}` would print
;      "Failed to replace env in config" warnings on EVERY `pnpm install` for
;      as long as the switch stays unset — which is the normal, dormant state.
;
; The workspace-root `.npmrc` is the only place `pnpm publish` will actually
; read a registry from (verified: it ignores `npm_config_*` env vars, and
; `publishConfig.registry` would outrank the switch — see
; scripts/guard-publish.mjs and docs/PUBLISHING.md).
;
; Placeholders substituted by scripts/release.mjs:
;   {{REGISTRY}}   ← the FAMS_NPM_REGISTRY env var
;   {{AUTH_KEY}}   ← //<host><path>/:_authToken derived from {{REGISTRY}}
;   {{TOKEN}}      ← the FAMS_NPM_TOKEN env var
; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@fams:registry={{REGISTRY}}
{{AUTH_KEY}}={{TOKEN}}
always-auth=true
